#18801
Mountain Trail~
   A small pebble tumbles uncontrollably down a steep mountainside nearby
to the north.  The pebble nearly hits you, but doesn't.  It bounces to a
stop in front of you, in the middle of the rocky trail you are on.  The
trail is a depressing mix of tan and gray colors.  Clouds of dust settle
on the mountainside, to be whipped up into swirling tornadoes of choking
dust whenever a soft breeze picks up; which happens every so often.  The
scent of stout yellowish green grass along with a mix of fresh flowers in
the air slowly begins to fade from memory to be replaced by a strenghtening
smell of damp earth and pine of a forest steadfastly growing to the east and
south.
