#18844
Beside a Small Stream~
   You come across a small crystal clear stream filled with ice cold, yet
refreshing water.  This stream must have surfaced nearby from a long journey
originating from the melting snows of some nearby mountains.  The stream will
probably reenter underground as part of its long journey west to the seacoast.
The ground here is soft and moist, growing under a few brown and withered
maple leaves is a thick layer of velvety moss.  You see ants crawling through
the moss' thick forest of sporophytes in the same way as you are bushwhacking
through this forest of oak and maple.
~
